# REGRESSION PIN — a `newtype` over `Box[int]`, the payload the whole track
# opened on, read back through the `*` deref.
#
# WRONG BEFORE THE FIX (measured at pristine HEAD, both backends): `gg build`
# rc 1. `register_newtype` read the inner type through the NON-registering
# `mapper.map_ast_type(...)`, so `Box[int]` was never registered and `_0`
# lowered to `Unit` — LLVM's `llc` refused ("void type only allowed for
# function results"), and the C lane truncated the payload pointer into a
# one-byte field.
#
# CORRECT AFTER THE FIX: `9` on C AND on LLVM. A cell that goes from
# "compiles on neither backend" to "correct on both" — reverting
# `register_newtype` ALONE brings rc 1 back on both, verified.
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE EXISTS BECAUSE THE FIRST ROUND OF A2's FIXTURE SET MISSED IT
# (Core #12). The set pinned `String`, `Vector[int]`, `Option[int]` and an enum
# payload, and named `Box` nowhere — while the track's own artifacts asserted
# that the `Box` cell had reached parity with its struct twin. An affirmative
# claim about a cell that no row pins is exactly the gap the fixture-coverage
# gate exists to catch.
#
# ⚠ THE READ SHAPE IS LOAD-BEARING — do not "simplify" it to `.get()`. The two
# reads have DIFFERENT outcomes and only this one is clean on both backends:
#
#     read shape        PRE C   PRE LLVM   POST C     POST LLVM
#     *(n.0)  (here)    rc 1    rc 1       9          9
#     n.0.get()         rc 1    rc 1       garbage    9
#
# The `.get()` row's residual C garbage is `todo/t1373` (a `Box[T].get()`
# through a STRUCT-FIELD receiver is handed the field's ADDRESS where the
# by-value `__get` expects the value), NOT this fix's: the struct control
# `known_gaps/box_get_through_struct_field_receiver_garbage.gg` prints the same
# garbage on C and the same `9` on LLVM at pristine HEAD, under every partial
# revert, and after the full fix. That INVARIANCE is what attributes the
# residual to `t1373`. Switching this fixture to `.get()` would park a known
# open defect in a live test.
newtype NX(Box[int])

void main():
    Box[int] b = Box(9)
    NX n = NX(^b)
    print(*(n.0))
